---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"leds\", \"colors\", \"write\"])"
---
Write a colours file (the JSON of `leds colors`) to the pad, live, with no reboot. Its colours become custom colours 0, 1, ...; the others become black. RAM only unless --save. gamepadii backs up the colours first. Every lights profile that uses colours 14 to 29 changes too

Usage: gamepadii leds colors write [OPTIONS] <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>
          The colours file, or - for standard input

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` and `leds` only
          
          [default: human]

      --save
          Also save them to flash

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --no-backup
          Don't back up the custom colours first

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --no-channel
          Don't use the USB control channel (the gamepadii firmware's): only web-config and button presses

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
